# Keep secrets out of the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` into the build stage. The final distroless
# image copies only the binary, so nothing here reaches production — but an
# intermediate layer that holds a private key is still a leaked private key the
# moment that layer is cached, pushed or exported.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
serviceAccountKey.json
gee-service-account.json
*.pem
*.key

# Not needed to build the Go binary, and node_modules alone is a large context.
frontend/
public/
node_modules/

# Build output and local state.
bin/
*.exe
*.log

# VCS and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Docs and fixtures — the binary does not read them.
docs/
*.md
*.pdf
*.sql
